+## FAQ
+
+### What are the best open source AI tools for small businesses in 2026?
+If you need broad business automation, start with `n8n`, `Dify`, `Flowise`, and `Activepieces`. If you need internal AI chat or document Q&A, start with `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, and `LibreChat`. If privacy and self-hosting matter most, `Ollama`, `LocalAI`, and `Jan` are the most practical entry points.
+
+### Which self-hosted AI tools are easiest for a small business to deploy?
+The easiest first deployments are usually `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, `Ollama`, `Jan`, and `n8n` because they have straightforward Docker or desktop setup paths. `Dify` and `Flowise` are also approachable, but they make more sense when you already know you need workflows, RAG, or agents.
+
+### Are there fully free AI tools for small businesses with public GitHub repos?
+Yes. Every item in this list has a public `github.com` repository. Some projects use permissive licenses like MIT or Apache-2.0, while others use source-available or copyleft licenses. The important distinction is that this list excludes proprietary SaaS-only tools and focuses on software you can inspect, self-host, and extend.
+
+### What is the best open source alternative to ChatGPT for a small business team?
+For a team chat experience, `LibreChat`, `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, and `Jan` are the most direct alternatives. The right choice depends on whether you want multi-user access, local model support, document ingestion, or a desktop-first workflow.
+
+### Which open source AI tools help small businesses automate workflows?
+`n8n`, `Activepieces`, `Flowise`, `Dify`, and `Langflow` are the strongest workflow-oriented options in this list. They differ in emphasis: `n8n` and `Activepieces` lean toward integrations and business automation, while `Dify`, `Flowise`, and `Langflow` lean more toward AI apps, agents, and RAG pipelines.
+
+### Are open source AI agent tools mature enough for small businesses?
+Partially. `CrewAI`, `Letta`, `OpenHands`, `Open Interpreter`, and `CopilotKit` are promising, but agent tooling still demands more technical oversight than classic SMB software. Small businesses should generally start with chat, knowledge search, or workflow automation before adopting fully autonomous agents.
