+# Contributing
+
+Thanks for contributing to `awesome-best-ai-tools-for-small-businesses-2026`.
+
+## Submission Rules
+
+1. Every submission must include a public `github.com` repository URL.
+2. No proprietary SaaS-only products.
+3. No listings without a verifiable GitHub repository.
+4. Include current GitHub metadata:
+   - stars
+   - primary language
+   - license
+   - last commit or latest visible repository activity date
+5. Keep the description grounded in the repository README and actual project scope.
+6. Explain why the tool is relevant to small-business AI use cases.
+7. If a category is weak, document the gap honestly instead of stretching the definition.
+
+## Recommended Process
+
+1. Fork the repository.
+2. Add or update entries in `README.md`.
+3. Verify formatting and links.
+4. Open a pull request with a short summary of what changed.
+
+## Quality Standard
+
+- Prefer tools that are actively maintained.
+- Prefer tools with clear installation docs.
+- Prefer tools that can realistically be adopted by small teams.
