+## TL;DR
+- `n8n`, `Dify`, and `Flowise` are the strongest all-around picks for small teams that need AI workflows, automations, and integrations without buying closed SaaS.
+- `Open WebUI`, `AnythingLLM`, and `LibreChat` are practical starting points for internal AI chat, document Q&A, and private knowledge assistants.
+- `Ollama`, `LocalAI`, and `Jan` are useful for local or self-hosted model access when privacy, offline use, or predictable cost matters.
+- `LiteLLM`, `Langfuse`, `Helicone`, `Phoenix`, and `Mem0` help small businesses manage spend, reliability, observability, and memory as AI systems mature.
+- Agent frameworks are still more technical than classic SMB software, but `CrewAI`, `Letta`, `OpenHands`, `Open Interpreter`, and `CopilotKit` are the clearest open source options to watch.
+
+## Why This List
+Most “best AI tools for small businesses” roundups mix proprietary SaaS, closed APIs, and vendor lock-in. This list does the opposite: every entry is a public GitHub repository, every tool is open source or source-available, and every pick is relevant to a real small-business workflow such as customer support, internal search, content operations, process automation, or private AI deployment. Where the category is still thin, that gap is stated plainly instead of padded with unrelated software.
